 up  in a better neighborhood the application  process it was a lottery and it was just  an overwhelming response but what the  builders did is they put in a poor door  so if you qualified for the subsidized  rental you entered in a different door  then the regular paying residents and  this isn't actually uncommon this is the  way that in England and we live there as  well that the mixed income communities  were structured so this is a very kind  of blatant example how communities can  be built in ways that are isolating and  reinforced the economic distance and  this is a pretty simple fix right and  many of you are probably doing much more  complicated sensitive things to reduce  that distance but just in terms of  building the physical environment in  this way you know kind of violates  almost everything we know about building  a sense of belonging and inclusivity and  and feeling like people can own the  space that they're in so with that I  just want to stop and kind of thank the  wonderful people that have have worked  on this project and went through that  fairly quickly but I want to make sure  that there was time and then if people  want all the papers are on our website  and adapt lab org so I welcome you to go  check that out  you
 

